<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?>
<!--
  <summary>
  SKIP-PILL, item 16 phase F (08/11/2026). The skip pill: bottom right over
  an intro, a recap or, when asked for, the end credits the Jellyfin server
  has marked, a button labelled Skip Intro, Skip Recap or Skip Credits with
  a bar along its foot that empties as the part plays. OK skips to the end
  of the part, Back hides the pill for it.
  </summary>
  <remarks>
  Off unless Skin.HasSetting(skip_pill). Not a dialog with a visible
  condition like the start badge: a dialog Kodi opens that way never has
  the focus, and this one has to take OK. service.py opens it itself as a
  modal WindowXMLDialog (update_skip_pill, _skip_pill_dialog_class), the
  next episode card's pattern, sets SkipPill.Label on it and moves the bar
  through the progress control. Drawn as the OSD's own buttons are (a flat
  plate in the accent, 56 tall, centred text), on Rob's request of
  09/11/2026: the first, rounded pill looked worse than the Jellyfin
  add-on's prompt. The label and the bar take Text on Accent's colour, so
  both read on a light accent too. The OSD and info keys close it to be
  passed on; pause, stop and volume reach the player by themselves.
  </remarks>
-->
<window type="dialog">
	<defaultcontrol always="true">9361</defaultcontrol>
	<animation effect="fade" time="200" condition="!Skin.HasSetting(reduce_motion)">WindowOpen</animation>
	<animation effect="fade" time="200" condition="!Skin.HasSetting(reduce_motion)">WindowClose</animation>
	<controls>
		<control type="group">
			<left>1580</left>
			<top>944</top>
			<width>280</width>
			<height>56</height>
			<control type="button" id="9361">
				<left>0</left>
				<top>0</top>
				<width>280</width>
				<height>56</height>
				<font>font_reg</font>
				<textcolor>$VAR[AccentTextColor]</textcolor>
				<focusedcolor>$VAR[AccentTextColor]</focusedcolor>
				<disabledcolor>disabled</disabledcolor>
				<align>center</align>
				<aligny>center</aligny>
				<textoffsety>-2</textoffsety>
				<texturefocus colordiffuse="$VAR[AccentColor]">white.png</texturefocus>
				<texturenofocus colordiffuse="$VAR[AccentColor]">white.png</texturenofocus>
				<label>$INFO[Window.Property(SkipPill.Label)]</label>
				<onleft>9361</onleft>
				<onright>9361</onright>
				<onup>9361</onup>
				<ondown>9361</ondown>
			</control>
			<!-- The bar: the share of the part still to play, the full
			     width of the button along its foot. -->
			<control type="progress" id="9362">
				<left>0</left>
				<top>52</top>
				<width>280</width>
				<height>4</height>
				<texturebg colordiffuse="33000000">white.png</texturebg>
				<midtexture colordiffuse="$VAR[AccentTextColor]">white.png</midtexture>
				<overlaytexture>-</overlaytexture>
			</control>
		</control>
	</controls>
</window>
